1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,866
This is Hallow—not another AI tab, but an Agent OS installed on your PC.

2
00:00:04,866 --> 00:00:13,828
One command builds the private runtime, verifies every dependency, creates the workspace, starts the managed service, and opens the desktop.

3
00:00:13,828 --> 00:00:20,747
On Windows, macOS, Linux, or WSL, the agent comes to the machine where the work actually lives.

4
00:00:20,747 --> 00:00:23,671
Before the first mission, Hallow proves it is ready.

5
00:00:23,671 --> 00:00:25,401
The runtime is healthy.

6
00:00:25,401 --> 00:00:27,020
Memory is indexed.

7
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:28,448
Model routes are connected.

8
00:00:28,448 --> 00:00:30,055
Tool policy is active.

9
00:00:30,055 --> 00:00:31,339
Skills are verified.

10
00:00:31,339 --> 00:00:32,578
Recovery is armed.

11
00:00:32,578 --> 00:00:33,783
No vague promise.

12
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:35,513
A readiness check you can inspect.

13
00:00:35,513 --> 00:00:37,946
Now, ask for the outcome in plain English.

14
00:00:37,946 --> 00:00:46,863
Hallow recalls durable context, scopes the workspace, selects bounded tools, and turns one instruction into a mission that can continue beyond a single reply.

15
00:00:46,863 --> 00:00:48,013
Watch the work happen.

16
00:00:48,013 --> 00:00:49,118
Memory recall.

17
00:00:49,118 --> 00:00:50,714
Repository inspection.

18
00:00:50,714 --> 00:00:51,863
Controlled repair.

19
00:00:51,863 --> 00:00:52,979
Verification.

20
00:00:52,979 --> 00:00:54,263
Release preparation.

21
00:00:54,263 --> 00:00:56,607
Every important step becomes a trace.

22
00:00:56,607 --> 00:01:01,160
When the mission reaches an external action, policy stops it at the boundary.

23
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:02,633
That is what makes Hallow different.

24
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:04,453
The runtime lives on your PC.

25
00:01:04,453 --> 00:01:06,930
Memory persists beyond the conversation.

26
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:10,055
Intelligence can route between local and cloud models.

27
00:01:10,055 --> 00:01:14,888
Tools, MCP, and tested skills operate inside explicit boundaries.

28
00:01:14,888 --> 00:01:19,040
Policy lives outside the prompt, and the operator stays in control.

29
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:26,015
Before anything leaves the machine, you see the exact target, the proposed change, its evidence, and its risk.

30
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:27,578
Autonomy moves quickly.

31
00:01:27,578 --> 00:01:29,274
Consent remains human.

32
00:01:29,274 --> 00:01:33,058
And when work fails, Hallow does not hide the error behind another answer.

33
00:01:33,058 --> 00:01:40,390
It captures the trace, isolates the cause, tests a repair, resumes from a checkpoint, and verifies readiness again.

34
00:01:40,390 --> 00:01:43,716
In dry-run mode, nothing unsafe is applied.

35
00:01:43,716 --> 00:01:44,598
Your machine.

36
00:01:44,598 --> 00:01:45,468
Your memory.

37
00:01:45,468 --> 00:01:46,339
Your agent.

38
00:01:46,339 --> 00:01:47,756
Hallow Agent OS.

39
00:01:47,756 --> 00:01:52,232
Install the intelligence that keeps working—and keeps you in control.

